  "deviations": [
    {
      "symbol": "yaml_parse()",
      "php": "an alias inside the node its anchor names builds a recursive array of references",
      "reason": "Rust values cannot be recursive: such an alias is refused as unknown (false)"
    },
    {
      "symbol": "yaml_parse()",
      "php": "ext-yaml corrupts its heap when a document that defined an anchor has a block mapping under an explicit key (`?`) whose value is an unknown alias, and then fails to parse (`m: &m v\\n? q: *x\\n- b`): the process dies later with 'zend_mm_heap corrupted', or the corruption shows in later parses.",
      "reason": "Memory corruption is undefined behaviour with no answer to compare; Rust refuses the document like any unknown alias. The fuzz profile keeps explicit keys to their own lines (`? q: r`, `n: &n 1\\n? q: *n`, `? [a]\\n: b`), so their values are never an unknown alias (the alias's anchor comes on the line before)."
    }
  ]
